+# RECONSTRUCTION: the sty_b61d2066 draft as submitted for story create review
+# (the draft text itself was not preserved as an artifact; this is rebuilt from
+# the story's recorded title, body and acceptance criteria).
+
+title: A session started through a satelle agent launcher runs cloud commands as the Azure or AWS identity its agent profile names, signed in from the machine's [vars] secrets without satelle placing the long-lived secret in the agent's environment
+category: feature
+
+Premise: where a provider supports short-lived credentials, the agent receives
+only those (for example AWS STS session credentials through credential_process).
+Where a provider persists a credential in its own config (for example the Azure
+CLI's service-principal cache under AZURE_CONFIG_DIR), the plan states it per
+provider.
+
+Acceptance criteria:
+1. An agent profile can name a cloud identity for Azure and for AWS whose
+   credential is a `${NAME}` reference into [vars]. satelle validate rejects a
+   malformed identity entry, or one that holds a literal secret.
+2. A session started through a satelle launcher runs as the profile's identity.
+   A test with a faked provider CLI shows the identity selected, and a dogfood
+   run shows `az account show` / `aws sts get-caller-identity` reporting it.
+3. Where a provider supports short-lived credentials (AWS STS), the agent
+   receives only those. Where a provider persists a credential in its own
+   config, the help text names it per provider.
